  "reason": "All four completed experiments use singleprofile, so the effect of multiprofile is completely untested—this is the largest source of design uncertainty. The evidence shows RNA (scvi_n200) is the dominant signal (rna_only=0.520 vs image_only=0.208), and multimodal with resnet50+concat (config_011, 0.536) is the best result so far. config_050 keeps the same model setting, encoders (scvi_n200 + resnet50), and fusion (concat) as config_011 but switches to multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool). This isolates the profile-setting effect with minimal confounding: if multiprofile+avgpool substantially improves over 0.536, it justifies investing further in transformer aggregation and other multiprofile variants; if it does not, we can deprioritize the large multiprofile portion of the search space. Under a limited budget, resolving this binary question is more informative than testing a smaller-axis change like weighted vs concat fusion."
}

